  "diagnosis": "Each streaming lane scans every row of a tile and filters by its level range, so total row reads and branch misses grow with lanes; the 28-worker stream is no faster than 8 workers. The gather is not bandwidth-limited on Broadwell (under 1 GB/s per core at 1.0 IPC), and a level-cursor variant would read each row once with no reuse, so tiling would only reorder accesses. Both micro-benchmark arms use the portable build; the plugin's AVX/FMA gather kernels widen the gap. The tiled norms also lost at 4 and 28 workers.",
  "retained": "MAP projections, group statistics and dense norms keep the gather and per-block routes."
